  "confidence_note": "radial-sweep footprint -- reconstructs the enclosing polygon from wall-surface points, correct for typical rectangular/L-shaped rooms. Assumes the room is star-shaped from its centroid; may misbehave on deep narrow notches or C-shaped layouts. Ceiling height uses a tightest-band-first RANSAC plane search with an honest confidence score (0 = no ceiling plane found, height is a rough lower-bound fallback). Wall-length/area CIs are a placeholder error model (fixed close-range depth-noise assumption), not yet calibrated against ground truth. Opening detection is a gap-in-coverage heuristic: can miss real openings on sparse data, and can false-positive on furniture pressed against a wall (no RGB/semantic check yet to tell the two apart) -- treat opening_count as an upper bound."
